ng","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Multilingual from the start"}],["$","span","2",{"children":": While Llama was English-centric, Qwen-7B launched with strong Chinese, English, and Japanese capabilities"}]]}],["$","p","352",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"2. "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":" permissive licensing"}],["$","span","2",{"children":": Apache 2.0 for most models, enabling commercial use without restriction"}]]}],["$","p","353",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"3. "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Comprehensive family"}],["$","span","2",{"children":": From 0.5B to 72B parameters, covering edge devices to data centers"}]]}],["$","p","354",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"4. "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Active maintenance"}],["$","span","2",{"children":": Regular updates, clear documentation, responsive community support"}]]}],["$","p","355",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"5. "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Alibaba Cloud integration"}],["$","span","2",{"children":": Easy path from experimentation to production deployment"}]]}],["$","p","357",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"This open-source strategy creates a "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"developer funnel"}],["$","span","2",{"children":": researchers and hobbyists experiment with free Qwen models, enterprises pilot with self-hosted versions, and successful deployments convert to Alibaba Cloud API customers."}]]}],["$","hr","359",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","h2","361",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Social Voices: Enterprise and Developer Perspectives"}]]}],["$","h3","363",{"style":{"fontSize":"22px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"32px 0 16px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"From the Enterprise Community"}]]}],["$","blockquote","366",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"\"我们评估了Azure OpenAI、AWS Bedrock和阿里云通义千问，最后选了通义。不是因为模型最强，而是整体TCO（总拥有成本）低60%。对于年调用量几百亿token的企业，这个差距就是每年省几千万。\""}]]}]]}],["$","p","366",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":">"}]]}],["$","blockquote","369",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*\"We evaluated Azure OpenAI, AWS Bedrock, and Alibaba Cloud Tongyi Qianwen, and chose Tongyi in the end. Not because the model is the strongest, but because the total cost of ownership is 60% lower. For enterprises with annual usage of tens of billions of tokens, this gap means saving tens of millions per year.\"*"}]]}],["$","p","1",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"— @企业CIO张 · 知乎 · ❤️ 6.2k"}]]}]]}],["$","blockquote","371",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"\"通义千问在金融合规方面的能力被低估了。它能理解监管文件，自动检查合同条款，这些都是其他通用AI做不到的。阿里多年的金融云经验不是白积累的。\""}]]}]]}],["$","p","371",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":">"}]]}],["$","blockquote","374",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*\"Tongyi Qianwen's capabilities in financial compliance are underestimated. It can understand regulatory documents and automatically check contract clauses—things other general-purpose AI can't do. Alibaba's years of financial cloud experience aren't for nothing.\"*"}]]}],["$","p","1",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"— @金融科技从业者 · 即刻 · ❤️ 3.8k"}]]}]]}],["$","blockquote","376",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"\"作为在东南亚做电商的华人，通义千问+阿里云的方案确实比AWS便宜不少。但问题是本地技术支持不够，出了问题找谁？这是阿里国际化的短板。\""}]]}]]}],["$","p","376",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":">"}]]}],["$","blockquote","379",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*\"As a Chinese person doing e-commerce in Southeast Asia, the Tongyi Qianwen + Alibaba Cloud solution is indeed much cheaper than AWS. But the problem is insufficient local technical support—who do you turn to when something goes wrong? This is Alibaba's internationalization weakness.\"*"}]]}],["$","p","1",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"— @跨境卖家小李 · 小红书 · ❤️ 2.4k"}]]}]]}],["$","h3","380",{"style":{"fontSize":"22px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"32px 0 16px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"From the Developer Community"}]]}],["$","blockquote","383",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"\"Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct is my go-to model for Chinese NLP tasks. The performance on C-Eval and CMMLU is genuinely excellent, and the 128K context is enough for most real-world applications. The fact that it's fully open-source under Apache 2.0 is the cherry on top.\""}]]}]]}],["$","p","383",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":">"}]]}],["$","blockquote","386",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*\"Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct is my go-to model for Chinese NLP tasks. The performance on C-Eval and CMMLU is genuinely excellent, and the 128K context is enough for most real-world applications. The fact that it's fully open-source under Apache 2.0 is the cherry on top.\"*"}]]}],["$","p","1",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"— @NLP_Engineer · Hacker News · ❤️ 2.1k"}]]}]]}],["$","blockquote","388",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"\"The Qwen-VL multimodal model is surprisingly good at document understanding. I've used it to extract structured data from scanned PDFs with complex tables, and it outperformed GPT-4V on Chinese documents.\""}]]}]]}],["$","p","388",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":">"}]]}],["$","blockquote","391",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*\"The Qwen-VL multimodal model is surprisingly good at document understanding. I've used it to extract structured data from scanned PDFs with complex tables, and it outperformed GPT-4V on Chinese documents.\"*"}]]}],["$","p","1",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"— @DataEngineer_Shenzhen · GitHub · ❤️ 1.6k"}]]}]]}],["$","h3","392",{"style":{"fontSize":"22px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"32px 0 16px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Critical Perspectives"}]]}],["$","blockquote","395",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"\"阿里做AI的问题是太'重'了。每次产品发布都伴随着一堆云服务的捆绑销售，让人感觉很臃肿。相比之下，DeepSeek的简洁和开放更有吸引力。\""}]]}]]}],["$","p","395",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":">"}]]}],["$","blockquote","398",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*\"Alibaba's problem with AI is that it's too 'heavy.' Every product release comes bundled with a pile of cloud services, feeling bloated. In comparison, DeepSeek's simplicity and openness are more attractive.\"*"}]]}],["$","p","1",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"— @独立开发者 · V2EX · ❤️ 3.1k"}]]}]]}],["$","blockquote","400",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"\"通义千问的C端体验确实一般。和Kimi、豆包比，界面不够精致，功能也不够有趣。阿里可能本来就不适合做C端产品。\""}]]}]]}],["$","p","400",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":">"}]]}],["$","blockquote","403",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*\"Tongyi Qianwen's consumer experience is indeed mediocre. Compared to Kimi and Doubao, the interface isn't polished enough and features aren't interesting enough. Alibaba probably wasn't suited for consumer products to begin with.\"*"}]]}],["$","p","1",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"— @产品经理陈 · 即刻 · ❤️ 2.7k"}]]}]]}],["$","blockquote","405",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"\"Qwen的开源策略很聪明，但有一个风险：如果社区发现其他开源模型（比如Llama 4或Mistral Large）性能更好，迁移成本很低。开源用户的忠诚度不如付费用户。\""}]]}]]}],["$","p","405",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":">"}]]}],["$","blockquote","408",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*\"Qwen's open-source strategy is smart, but there's a risk: if the community finds other open-source models (like Llama 4 or Mistral Large) perform better, migration costs are low. Open-source user loyalty is less than paid users.\"*"}]]}],["$","p","1",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"— @开源观察者 · 知乎 · ❤️ 1.9k"}]]}]]}],["$","hr","409",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","h2","411",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Challenges and Risks"}]]}],["$","h3","413",{"style":{"fontSize":"22px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"32px 0 16px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Technical Challenges"}]]}],["$","p","415",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"1. Competition from DeepSeek:"}]]}],["$","p","416",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"DeepSeek's cost efficiency threatens Tongyi's pricing:"}]]}],["$","p","417",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"- Enterprise clients cost-sensitive at scale"}]]}],["$","p","418",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"- API costs are major line item for AI-heavy applications"}]]}],["$","p","419",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"- Tongyi must reduce costs or justify premium"}]]}],["$","p","421",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"2. Consumer Mindshare:"}]]}],["$","p","422",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"- Less viral than Wenxin Yiyan or Kimi"}]]}],["$","p","423",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"- Perceived as \"enterprise tool\" not \"daily assistant\""}]]}],["$","p","424",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"- Risk of losing consumer-driven innovation"}]]}],["$","p","426",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"3. Model Performance Gap:"}]]}],["$","p","427",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"While Qwen2.5-Max is competitive, it doesn't consistently lead benchmarks. On coding tasks, DeepSeek and Kimi often outperform. On creative tasks, Claude maintains advantages. Tongyi's strength is reliability and integration, not raw capability."}]]}],["$","h3","429",{"style":{"fontSize":"22px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"32px 0 16px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Strategic Risks"}]]}],["$","p","431",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"1. Geopolitical Tensions:"}]]}],["$","p","432",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"- US-China tech competition affects:"}]]}],["$","p","433",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"  - International expansion"}]]}],["$","p","434",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"  - Access to advanced chips"}]]}],["$","p","435",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"  - Enterprise trust outside China"}]]}],["$","p","437",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"2. Regulatory Environment:"}]]}],["$","p","438",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"- China's AI regulations continue evolving"}]]}],["$","p","439",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"- Compliance costs increasing"}]]}],["$","p","440",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"- International standards fragmentation"}]]}],["$","p","442",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"3. Open Source Competition:"}]]}],["$","p","443",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"- Qwen models are partially open, but lag DeepSeek's full openness"}]]}],["$","p","444",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"- Enterprise preference for vendor independence"}]]}],["$","p","445",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"- Risk of community momentum shifting to fully open alternatives"}]]}],["$","p","447",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"4. Organizational Complexity:"}]]}],["$","p","448",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Alibaba's massive scale (220,000+ employees) creates coordination challenges. Tongyi must compete for resources with e-commerce, cloud, logistics, and entertainment divisions. The \"startup within a giant\" dynamic can slow decision-making and product iteration."}]]}],["$","hr","450",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","h2","452",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Conclusion: The Enterprise Choice"}]]}],["$","p","454",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Tongyi Qianwen represents Alibaba's strategic vision for AI: not just a chatbot, but the intelligent layer connecting China's digital commerce, cloud infrastructure, and enterprise workflows. With 30,000 enterprise clients and deep integration into the Alibaba ecosystem, it has established itself as the practical choice for businesses building AI into their operations."}]]}],["$","p","456",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The trade-off is clear: Tongyi sacrifices some of the viral consumer appeal of Wenxin Yiyan and the technical innovation spotlight of DeepSeek in exchange for enterprise reliability, compliance, and ecosystem integration. For businesses—especially those already in the Alibaba ecosystem—this is often the right trade-off."}]]}],["$","p","458",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"For international observers, Tongyi Qianwen demonstrates that China's AI landscape isn't monolithic. While DeepSeek grabs headlines with efficiency and Baidu captures consumers with distribution, Alibaba is building the enterprise backbone that powers China's digital economy. Each plays a distinct role in the ecosystem."}]]}],["$","p","460",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"As AI becomes infrastructure rather than novelty, Tongyi's cloud-native, enterprise-first approach may prove prescient. The question isn't whether Alibaba can make AI cool—it's whether they can make AI indispensable to how Chinese businesses operate."}]]}],["$","p","462",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The bet is that, in the long run, indispensability beats coolness."}]]}],["$","hr","464",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","p","466",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Related Articles:"}]]}],["$","p","467",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"- "}],["$","a","1",{"href":"/blog/china-ai-global-surge-api-traffic-empire-2026/","style":{"color":"#22d3ee","textDecoration":"underline"},"children":"China's AI Revolution: How 140 Trillion Tokens, DeepSeek V4 on Huawei Chips, and a $700B Arms Race Are Reshaping Global Technology"}]]}],["$","p","468",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"- "}],["$","a","1",{"href":"/blog/deepseek-v4-promo-ending-analysis/","style":{"color":"#22d3ee","textDecoration":"underline"},"children":"DeepSeek V4's 75% Promo Ends May 31: What Happens Next and Why the AI Pricing War Is Just Beginning"}]]}],["$","p","469",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"- "}],["$","a","1",{"href":"/blog/china-ai-global-surge-api-traffic-empire-2026/","style":{"color":"#22d